1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,752
Long ago, in a forest school, Guru Drona taught the young princes.

2
00:00:05,752 --> 00:00:08,763
One morning, he set them a test.

3
00:00:08,813 --> 00:00:12,750
High on a tree, he placed a small wooden bird.

4
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:15,331
“Aim for its eye,” he said.

5
00:00:15,331 --> 00:00:18,464
“But first, tell me… what do you see?”

6
00:00:18,614 --> 00:00:21,659
The eldest prince raised his bow.

7
00:00:21,659 --> 00:00:26,141
“I see the tree, the branches, the leaves… and my brothers.”

8
00:00:26,141 --> 00:00:28,184
“Step aside.”

9
00:00:28,234 --> 00:00:31,896
The next saw the sky, the bird, and his teacher.

10
00:00:31,896 --> 00:00:33,889
“Step aside.”

11
00:00:33,889 --> 00:00:37,245
One by one, they all stepped aside.

12
00:00:37,395 --> 00:00:39,741
Then came Arjuna.

13
00:00:39,741 --> 00:00:41,420
“What do you see?”

14
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,911
“I see only the bird.”

15
00:00:44,161 --> 00:00:46,011
“Look closer.”

16
00:00:46,342 --> 00:00:48,348
“Only its eye.”

17
00:00:48,398 --> 00:00:50,248
“Then shoot.”

18
00:00:52,091 --> 00:00:54,739
The arrow found its mark.

19
00:00:54,739 --> 00:00:58,900
Arjuna became the greatest archer of his age.

20
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:03,094
The world will always show you a hundred things.

21
00:01:03,094 --> 00:01:05,201
See only your goal,

22
00:01:05,201 --> 00:01:07,253
and you will hit it.

23
00:01:08,203 --> 00:01:10,775
Follow for more stories.
